From: Johannes Stein <johannesstein@freeze-dev.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 12:32:11 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 68/77] rtl: WASI: set up argc/argv at startup, objpas.ParamStr
 returned '' before the first ParamCount

The WASI system unit sets up argc/argv lazily (setup_arguments, called
from ParamCount and System.ParamStr). objpas.ParamStr, the AnsiString
version used in {$mode objfpc} and {$mode delphi}, reads argc/argv
directly, so in a program that calls ParamStr(1) before ParamCount it
saw argc=0 and returned '' for every parameter (ParamStr(0) worked, it
goes through System.ParamStr):

  {$mode objfpc} begin writeln(ParamStr(1)); end.   { empty under wasmtime p a }

Call setup_arguments in the system unit's initialization, next to
Setup_Environment.
---
 rtl/wasicommon/system.pp | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/rtl/wasicommon/system.pp b/rtl/wasicommon/system.pp
index 2ba1a48f..bd071ce2 100644
--- a/rtl/wasicommon/system.pp
+++ b/rtl/wasicommon/system.pp
@@ -528,6 +528,11 @@ begin
   { Setup stdin, stdout and stderr }
   SysInitStdIO;
   Setup_Environment;
+  { set up argc/argv now: objpas.ParamStr (the AnsiString version of
+    {$mode objfpc} and {$mode delphi}) reads them directly and does not call
+    setup_arguments, so before the first ParamCount/System.ParamStr call it
+    returned '' for every parameter }
+  setup_arguments;
   Setup_PreopenedDirs;
 {$ifdef FPC_WASM_THREADS}
   TLSInfoBlock:=Nil;
